I bought a Radeon 7500 PCI from knowledgemicro.com.  It came in a retail
box with PowerColor branding.  It is the version with both DVI and HD15
connectors.

short story:  it doesn't work in my 164LX.

With AlphaBIOS 5.70 it would allow the bios to run, but MILO 2.2-19 would
lock up on it.  I expected this based on other reports.

So... I upgraded my system to SRM 5.8, repartitioned my disks using
disklabel, installed aboot, setup devfs and LVM, removed the old noisy
SCSI boot disk, etc.  (a bunch of much needed maintenance).

When I put this card in, SRM's bios emulation locks up after displaying
the card bios's one cryptic line of numerical model/serial number goo.
I guess its time for me to review the list archives to see what exact
brand people report that -does- work.

-g



