I'd like to report success with software RAID1 on my PC164LX.  I know=20
some people were reporting failure with software raid on Alpha some=20
months ago.

I used stock kernel: 2.4.22-rc2 with a patch from=20
<http://www.spinics.net/lists/raid/msg02526.html>.  This patch is=20
absolutely required, or any I/O to the built raidset caused a kernel=20
oops.

I build raid1 and md as modules, which means I am unable to RAID my /=20
partition without hacking init scripts to do a chroot on boot (or using=20
an initrd, which I consider too much trouble).  I'm also not sure=20
autorecognition would work anyway, since I don't know how to mark a BSD=20
disklabel partition as part of a RAID (in DOS partition format, you use=20
partition type 'fd' but BSD disklabel partition types seem to only go=20
up to 0x10).  I'm also lucky that LX can boot off of its builtin IDE=20
controller, or I'd still need SCSI (or floppy :-) ).

All other filesystems are now off of two identical 120GB Maxtor IDE=20
drives.  Getting rid of the old, small, power-hungry SCSI drives (and=20
controller) has made my UPS much happier :-)

In order to boot aboot/SRM off of an IDE drive, I had to either=20
manually specifiy 'boot dqa0.0' or remove the second (slave) drive from=20
the primary IDE controller.  With the second drive present, 'b dqa0'=20
would give "Failed to send Read to dqa0' error messages.  This means=20
that auto_action boot did not work.  I'm not sure if this is specific=20
to my setup or not.

I also configured the root filesystem with 'mke2fs -j -O none' (i.e.=20
kernel 2.2-compatible ext2) for aboot's sake, though I don't know if=20
this was strictly necessary.

For the non-Alpha-specific parts, I followed the Software RAID HOWTO at=20
<http://www.tldp.org/HOWTO/Software-RAID-HOWTO.html>

